Fillets: a closed rounding walked over a gap in its face (the rounded
mouth of a hole the ball cannot touch, 0160) where the piece over the gap
runs on round most of the spine, or the gap lies across the spine's start
(mitcad#343).

The case: a disc's bottom rim rounded with 1 over a narrow rounding of the
rim (the edge overflow), the contact on the bottom face running over the
mouth of a blind hole near the rim, rounded with 0.5. The blend is walked
on over the gap and cut by the mouth's rounding, the cut crossing that
rounding's seam, so the piece is cut in two at the seam
(WalkedBridgeOverGap). Three faults:

- ChFi3d_KPartLineParam: the piece over the gap was walked from the gap on
  round the rest of the closed spine (its other contact's line from the
  gap's start to the spine's end), and the parameter on that line of the
  section through the gap's start, the line's own start, came from the
  projection's nearest foot on the far side of the disc: the line's ends
  were not taken as feet. The cut then found no crossing of the seam, the
  plain cut failed and so did the stripe. A bounded line's end nearer to
  the point than any foot is taken now.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutCurve: with the gap across the spine's start, the piece
  ends at the section where the contact comes back into its face, and the
  intersection of the walked blend with the mouth's rounding lost the last
  stretch of the cut at the surface's boundary there (the cut went round
  the long way). A walked blend (a B-spline) is intersected as extended by
  a quarter of its length past both ends along the spine.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece: with the gap across the spine's start, the stretch
  past the start took the vertex where the cut crossed the seam, just
  before that stretch, for a vertex of the face beyond under the blend
  (its nearest point on the contact's line was the line's end), and the
  piece was given up. A vertex whose nearest point on that line is no foot
  (it lies beyond the stretch along the spine) is passed over.

On the stored body before the item the rounding is now valid: a change of
volume of -7.38905 mm3 against the stored -7.38889, the mouth's rounding
5.6721 mm2 against 5.6708; on the replay's body (whose spine starts in the
gap) -7.38891. The disc in geometry/tests/test_fillet_end_overflow.cpp
fails without the third change (the gap across the spine's start on either
side of it); the first two are verified on the stored body and the replay's
body only, as no synthetic body made the projection miss the line's end or
the intersection lose its last stretch.

Upstream: new.
